  "body": "Hi.\nI installed successfully _agx-emulsion_ in Windows as I described [here](https://discuss.pixls.us/t/spectral-film-simulations-in-art/48442/48)\nThen I created the subdir:\n_C:\\Users\\%username%\\AppData\\Local\\ART\\FilmSimulation_\nwhere I put **agx_emulsion_mklut.py** and **ART_agx_film.json**\n\nAt this point I went to the **ART Preferences** and at the level of **Image Processing > Directories > CLUT directory** I set _FilmSimulation_ as default dir.\nAfter that I loaded an image into ART and, from the dropdown menu **Mode** of the _LocalEditing tab > Color/Tone Correction > Mode_, I choosed  **LUT**.\n\nAs soon as I choose LUT, on the image to be processed appears the statement:\n\"**Color/Tone Correction - Error reading file: (None)**\"\nas shown in the image below.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4aa1152b-9c3d-4c39-a7e5-182c18679a86)\n\nThis warning disappears as soon as the presence of a LUT file is recognized into the FilmSimulation directory.\n\n**Question**: is it possible to delay the apperance of the message (for example 10\") giving the time to the program to load the LUT file?\nThis is not a big problem at all, but if this statement doesn't appear is more elegant, IMHO.\n\nBTW my computer is quite fast, but the statement remains for 3-4\" on the screen.\n\nRegards,\nTopoldo/Leopoldo\n",
